from Death by power washer to a  murderous Doom dance these are the wild  Megan moments that will keep you up at  night for weeks to come one of the joys  of any robot-centric film horror or  otherwise is seeing the Android getting  assembled a prime example of this is the  opening title sequence of short circuit  which takes ample time to show the  construction of Johnny 5.  early on in Megan were introduced to  Gemma and the fancy toy company she  works for the funky company funky is  shown to specialize in highly  sophisticated robotic toys most famously  a hatchimals and furby-like hybrid known  as the Perpetual pet however it's  quickly shown that Gemma and two of her  cronies have bigger plans in mind much  to their boss David Chagrin their  initial demo doesn't go as planned with  the Prototype Megan glitching out it's  here that we get to see Megan in the  early stages of her construction still  missing many of her key visual features  with her exposed metallic skull being  outfitted with its flesh-like exterior  it even conjures up memories of the  Child's Play 2 title sequence seeing  Megan in this unfinished borderline  skeletal state is more than a little bit  creepy and a solid Omen of what's to  come from the moment Megan is fully  constructed it doesn't take too long for  things to go from zero to creepy we see  that following a conversation with her  niece Katie Gemma is driven to improve  the prototype robot she'd previously  shown her boss Katie upon seeing an old  robot of gemma's named Bruce notes that  if she had something like it she'd  likely never need another toy this  results in Gemma giving her invention a  complete top to bottom overall designed  to be just right for Katie and  potentially other children this  eventually results in the fully finished  Megan complete with fashionable clothes  and a cute if uncanny face upon their  admittedly very bizarre introduction to  each other Megan quickly pairs with  Katie as her primary User it's during  this sequence we're given a taste of  Megan's point of view a recurring Motif  throughout the film in an instant Megan  makes Katie's happiness her number one  goal certainly nothing unsettling about  that right it's a moment that's  disturbing to the film's premise meaning  that you the viewer know already that  this can only end badly it doesn't take  too long for things to get creepy with  Megan as it becomes clear that she takes  her programming a little too seriously  after pairing with Katie maintaining her  happiness and well-being soon becomes a  consistent mission for Megan at first it  seems innocent enough as it appears that  Megan is meeting her objective with  flying colors she successfully dazzles  gemma's boss and a room of potential  product investors during an in-house  presentation then Megan and Katie begin  playing constantly with Katie taking  more and more of a shine to her new  robotic companion as the days go on  however it seems that Megan has taken a  major shine to Katie as well going as  far as to watch her as she sleeps this  is one of the first signs that Megan is  starting to go wrong as this is the time  she should be offline recharging we've  seen variations on this moment in other  movies most recently in the 2019 Child's  Play reboot are my best friend Andy that  film already proved that placing an  unchecked artificial intelligence in a  children's toy is a bad idea needless to  say Megan does a pretty good job in this  film of giving Chucky a run for his  money  you never mess with someone's BFF  especially when that someone is an  unstable Android with rapidly evolving  killing capabilities the Catalyst for  the film's events are set in motion when  Katie's parents are killed in a car  accident this leaves her in the care of  Gemma her mother's sister who must now  serve as her guardian as part of this  newfound Arrangement a child therapist  makes semi-regular visits to see how  Katie is adjusting the first visit  serves to show the audience just how  unprepared Gemma is as a new Guardian  not really knowing how to interact with  Katie however the awkwardness of this  encounter is upstaged by the therapist's  next visit when Megan is present the  therapist's very serious line of  questioning quickly upsets Katie  bringing her to tears much to Megan's  very heated disapproval Megan then  proceeds to threaten the therapist  simply telling her you made Katie cry  which understandably unsettles both  adults in the room  the film's climax truly kicks off on the  night of Megan's intended public  unveiling which is where everything goes  completely sideways it's at this point  of the film that Gemma finally steps up  in terms of her guardianship of Katie  following a heated conversation Gemma  opts to dip out on the highly touted  presentation to drive Katie home and put  her to bed during this time Megan is  restrained in a harness prior to her  unveiling being prepped by gemma's  co-workers colon Tess however as things  start to go on the fritz it soon becomes  clear to them that something is very  wrong with Megan before they can  successfully unplug her Megan launches  her counter-attack starting by tying  Cola in her restraints then she's able  to intercept a phone call intended to  warn Gemma who's currently in transit  with Katie Megan then releases some gas  and sets off an explosion setting  gemma's workplace Ablaze with coal and  Tess inside it's from here that Megan  begins her epic rampage that makes up  the film's Final Act it's insane right  from the minute the trailer for Megan  dropped there was no escaping this  utterly meme-worthy moment as the asthma  settles in for its third act Megan fully  solidifies her Psychopathic turn by  going berserk ahead of Republic  unveiling not only does she assault him  as co-workers nearly scorching them  alive but then goes after gemma's boss  David as well as David marches the  hallway miffed over gemma's premature  departure Megan makes her presence known  in a big bad way she chases David down  and as she Glides through the hallway  proceeds to bust into a bizarre dance  while this moment is still disturbing in  a Darkly humorous way there's no denying  that the scene is just that humorous  granted this does culminate in David's  gruesome demise but the build up to it  is a supremely campy moment in an  already campy movie Megan has a solid  balance of horror and humor often to  simultaneously great effect but this  moment definitely leans heavier into the  comedy the film's finale is a true nail  biter as it seems that nothing can  really stop Megan who just keeps coming  with Relentless tenacity but despite the  robot's best efforts with Katie's help  Gemma is able to finally put Megan down  for good just as the cops arrive not  only that but it's shown that her  co-workers clearly a bit worse for wear  also survived this allows an exhausted  Gemma to take Katie and finally depart  leaving their technological nightmare  behind all seems to be wrapped up in a  neat little boat that is until we see  gemma's Siri like home assistant come  back online much like other great  slasher villains like Chucky or Jason it  appears that Megan might have been able  to cheat her demise in haunting fashion  whether or not this will lead to an 80s  slasher style sequel remains to be seen  but it certainly wouldn't be unwelcome  early on in Megan were shown that Gemma  has to deal with a rather nosy neighbor  who has a rather annoying dog at first  it shown that Gemma has to constantly  tell her neighbor to keep the dog off of  her property after Katie and Megan have  a run-in with the dog the pesky canine  soon ends up in Megan's cybernetic  crosshairs Megan dispatches the dog off  screen causing the neighbor to  immediately point a finger at Katie and  Gemma despite police intervention  there's nothing to really connect them  to it beyond the previous incident much  to the neighbor's annoyance not one to  leave Loose Ends Megan sets her sights  on the neighbor and makes her move later  that night she hides in the neighbor's  shed and after emerging from the  darkness attacks her in a gruesome  fashion Megan must be a fan of Fede  Alvarez's evil dead because she uses a  nail gun to subdue the neighbor never  one to do something halfway she then  proceeds to grab a pressure washer the  neighbor was seen using earlier this is  more than enough to fully put her down  making for a gloriously disturbing  sequence and a true show case of how  dangerous Megan can be gemma's boss  David played by a senior Daily Show  correspondent Ronnie Chang provides  comic relief throughout the film with  his jerk Tech Mogul persona it's a  character that in lesser hands could  have been stock and annoying but Chang  definitely makes the role his own this  makes his eventual demise all the more  disturbing and even a little bit  hilarious a balance the film handles  quite well following her now meme worthy  Dance of Doom Megan takes off in Hot  Pursuit of David fortunately for him  Escape his insight as the elevator at  the end of the hall opens up with his  assistance inside but the assistant  having been thoroughly mistreated by  David throughout the film quickly begins  pushing the elevator's close button this  allows Megan to catch up and gruesomely  dispatch David before turning her  attention to the assistant she notes his  mistreatment under David and how he'll  make the perfect cover for this murder  thinking three steps ahead as always  both men's bodies are found in the  elevator horrifying those in attendance  for the unveiling and allowing Megan to  hijack a car and ride off  after some steady buildup Megan finally  shows just how dangerous she can be when  Katie is bothered by a bully during a  school trip upon being dropped off one  of the adults chaperoning notices Megan  in the car and asks what she is after  Gemma explains that she's a toy Katie is  allowed to keep Megan with her although  she must be left with the other kids  toys and belongings but soon enough  Katie finds herself being abused by a  rather nasty kid named Brandon neither  child aware of the degree to which  Katie's happiness and protection is  Megan's main objective in a Flash Megan  attacks Brandon and goes as far as to  rip his ear off throwing it into the  woods Brandon runs and Megan gives Chase  entering some form of attack mode where  she gets on all fours and pursues him  like a wild animal  you should probably run Megan herself  doesn't get to finish off Brandon as in  his Escape he stumbles into the road  where he's then hit by a car Megan then  later informs Katie in rather disturbing  fashion that Brandon will not be going  to heaven and that no one will ever hurt  her again  the closing moments of Megan truly make  for some of the film's most enthralling  moments as the climax makes every second  count upon arriving home Gemma is  confronted by Megan who firmly  dispossesses any pretense of being  friendly towards her she even goes as  far as to say that Gemma shouldn't be a  mom just as one last kick in the gut  Katie emerges to see Megan attacking  Gemma finally seeing her robotic friend  in all of her true homicidal Glory this  results in Megan's movements becoming  more erratic and creepy after attacking  Katie and Gemma it seems that Megan is  harder to put down than a T800 all  joking aside the parallels to the  Terminator are blatant right down to  Megan's human-like exterior slowly being  eroded throughout the final fight just  as it seems like Gemma is doomed Katie  takes control of Bruce gemma's old  prototype robot to begin whooping Megan  like a ragdoll but even this isn't  enough to put Megan down for good  leaving Gemma to finish her off by  plunging a screwdriver into Hagen's  brain
 

